WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.233 --> 00:00:03.039
Hey, Conan 360 Live,
this is John Kourounis

00:00:03.039 --> 00:00:04.734
from Warner Brothers
Studios Tour Hollywood,

00:00:04.734 --> 00:00:06.992
and I'm currently in the
Warner Brothers Archive Museum

00:00:06.992 --> 00:00:08.815
in the Harry Potter exhibit.

00:00:08.815 --> 00:00:10.174
So, let's take a look.

00:00:10.174 --> 00:00:11.537
First of all, see that owl.

00:00:11.537 --> 00:00:14.506
We trained it to stay
perfectly, perfectly still.

00:00:14.506 --> 00:00:16.600
It's acting like a security guard for us.

00:00:16.600 --> 00:00:17.710
We also have the fireplace,

00:00:17.710 --> 00:00:20.329
where Harry receives his
letter to go to Hogwarts,

00:00:20.329 --> 00:00:21.611
he just wants to get an education

00:00:21.611 --> 00:00:23.840
and be a good person, that's it.

00:00:23.840 --> 00:00:25.832
We have first edition Harry Potter books

00:00:25.832 --> 00:00:26.856
signed by JK Rowling.

00:00:26.856 --> 00:00:28.220
Don't try to take these out of the case

00:00:28.220 --> 00:00:30.187
because there's an alarm on it.

00:00:30.187 --> 00:00:33.327
And as you can see, we also
have a Fantastic Beasts section.

00:00:33.327 --> 00:00:34.901
We're gonna get to that.

00:00:34.901 --> 00:00:36.341
Now, we're gonna take a walk around

00:00:36.341 --> 00:00:38.385
and check out some of my
absolute favorite things

00:00:38.385 --> 00:00:40.162
from all eight Harry Potter movies,

00:00:40.162 --> 00:00:42.760
and also Fantastic Beasts
And Where To Find Them.

00:00:42.760 --> 00:00:43.875
Let's go check it out.

00:00:43.875 --> 00:00:45.574
Currently, we're in the Harry
Potter part of our exhibit

00:00:45.574 --> 00:00:46.951
at the Warner Brothers Archive.

00:00:46.951 --> 00:00:48.869
Now, truth be told, the
greatest part about all of this

00:00:48.869 --> 00:00:50.701
is that's it's all the real deal,

00:00:50.701 --> 00:00:52.037
these are the real costumes, real props

00:00:52.037 --> 00:00:54.838
used in the productions, so
really worn by the actors

00:00:54.838 --> 00:00:56.780
and the props really used.

00:00:56.780 --> 00:00:58.484
Now, if you look all the way over here.

00:00:58.484 --> 00:01:00.438
In Chamber of Secrets,
you not only meet Aragog,

00:01:00.438 --> 00:01:02.129
but all of the descendants of Aragog.

00:01:02.129 --> 00:01:03.587
If you have arachnophobia, don't look.

00:01:03.587 --> 00:01:06.388
But real spider, the Acromantula.

00:01:06.388 --> 00:01:08.224
We also have a Quidditch exhibit

00:01:08.224 --> 00:01:09.709
and the Quidditch exhibit is not complete

00:01:09.709 --> 00:01:12.578
without, of course, a
Nimbus 2000, right here.

00:01:12.578 --> 00:01:15.073
Now, on this side we have original

00:01:15.073 --> 00:01:19.240
Harry, Ron and Hermione
costumes, truly used in action.

00:01:19.719 --> 00:01:21.217
They verified it.

00:01:21.217 --> 00:01:24.282
And the greatest professors of Hogwarts.

00:01:24.282 --> 00:01:26.978
We have Rubeus Hagrid,
we have Professor Snape,

00:01:26.978 --> 00:01:29.813
we have Professor Dumbledore, McGonagall,

00:01:29.813 --> 00:01:32.569
Professor Flitwick, I
want to go to Hogwarts.

00:01:32.569 --> 00:01:34.460
But if you go to Hogwarts, you have to

00:01:34.460 --> 00:01:36.344
get sorted in your house, right?

00:01:36.344 --> 00:01:39.452
And guys, this is the real Sorting Sat.

00:01:39.452 --> 00:01:42.572
So you come here, this is the experience.

00:01:42.572 --> 00:01:46.440
Wear the Sorting Hat,
find out where you belong.

00:01:46.440 --> 00:01:48.935
(blows breath) What's it gonna be?

00:01:48.935 --> 00:01:52.843
(Harry Potter music)

00:01:52.843 --> 00:01:55.281
[Sorting Hat] Conscientious
and hardworking,

00:01:55.281 --> 00:01:56.948
a great thing to be.

00:01:58.249 --> 00:01:59.166
Hufflepuff!

00:02:00.025 --> 00:02:01.598
Hufflepuff?

00:02:01.598 --> 00:02:04.343
(sighs) Supposed to be Gryffindor.

00:02:04.343 --> 00:02:07.541
My parents are not gonna
be happy, that's fine.

00:02:07.541 --> 00:02:09.685
And you can't talk about Harry
Potter without talking about

00:02:09.685 --> 00:02:12.724
the Dark Lord, himself, Lord Voldemort.

00:02:12.724 --> 00:02:14.106
If you back up all the way over here,

00:02:14.106 --> 00:02:15.882
we even have their wands.

00:02:15.882 --> 00:02:17.776
Now remember, the wizard
doesn't choose the wand,

00:02:17.776 --> 00:02:19.708
the wand chooses the wizard.

00:02:19.708 --> 00:02:22.176
We have the adult Voldemort, cool right?

00:02:22.176 --> 00:02:25.471
We've got teenage Tom Riddle,
we also have young Tom Riddle

00:02:25.471 --> 00:02:27.932
long before he is Lord Voldemort.

00:02:27.932 --> 00:02:31.164
Now if you guys can see all the
way back here, that's Dobby.

00:02:31.164 --> 00:02:32.836
Now, Dobby didn't actually exists on set,

00:02:32.836 --> 00:02:34.341
he was completely done in post production.

00:02:34.341 --> 00:02:36.182
So this is like a recreation so that they

00:02:36.182 --> 00:02:37.736
kind had a point of reference.

00:02:37.736 --> 00:02:40.129
Most of the time when they would
interact with Dobby on set,

00:02:40.129 --> 00:02:41.871
they would talk to a tennis ball.

00:02:41.871 --> 00:02:43.846
Random, I know.

00:02:43.846 --> 00:02:44.905
Now, for those of you guys

00:02:44.905 --> 00:02:47.035
that are big fans, excuse me, my dear,

00:02:47.035 --> 00:02:49.252
we have Sirius Black, Gary Oldman.

00:02:49.252 --> 00:02:50.997
Here's a fun tour fact for you.

00:02:50.997 --> 00:02:54.074
Gary Oldman came to take the tour one time

00:02:54.074 --> 00:02:55.125
and he was on the back of a cart,

00:02:55.125 --> 00:02:57.175
nobody knew on the cart who he was,

00:02:57.175 --> 00:02:59.087
which is hilarious to me.

00:02:59.087 --> 00:03:00.888
The world of Harry Potter
is not complete, either,

00:03:00.888 --> 00:03:03.598
without talking about how
artistic and fantastic and magical

00:03:03.598 --> 00:03:07.252
the whole thing is, and we even
have some of their original

00:03:07.252 --> 00:03:09.020
machetes of Fluffy the Three-headed Dog,

00:03:09.020 --> 00:03:11.015
the Basilisk, the Hippogriff.

00:03:11.015 --> 00:03:13.307
And even these things
that don't wind up on set,

00:03:13.307 --> 00:03:15.881
you still have to create
them so that you have an idea

00:03:15.881 --> 00:03:17.667
of what your world really looks like.

00:03:17.667 --> 00:03:21.834
So, in my mind, this is a
tribute to true artists.

00:03:22.363 --> 00:03:23.931
Now we're in the Fantastic Beasts

00:03:23.931 --> 00:03:25.547
And Where To Find Them section.

00:03:25.547 --> 00:03:29.629
We are standing in the presence
of Oscar winners my friends.

00:03:29.629 --> 00:03:31.262
Take a look behind you.

00:03:31.262 --> 00:03:33.706
This is a recreation of
Jacob Kowalski's apartment.

00:03:33.706 --> 00:03:35.265
Dan Fogler played that character.

00:03:35.265 --> 00:03:36.492
So you see the suit that he actually

00:03:36.492 --> 00:03:39.259
wore to the bank to try to
get the loan, you see his bed,

00:03:39.259 --> 00:03:41.682
the briefcase that sets
the whole thing off.

00:03:41.682 --> 00:03:44.376
Is there a fantastic
beast in there? Who knows.

00:03:44.376 --> 00:03:46.384
But you can see the open
one with the biscuits.

00:03:46.384 --> 00:03:48.965
Don't try to eat them,
they're stale, I tried.

00:03:48.965 --> 00:03:52.874
So his apartment is an absolute
disaster, kind of like mine.

00:03:52.874 --> 00:03:54.963
In the distance you also see
Eddie Redmayne's character,

00:03:54.963 --> 00:03:57.358
Newt Scamander, he's the
man, the myth, the legend.

00:03:57.358 --> 00:04:00.132
Really, the focal point
of the entire movie.

00:04:00.132 --> 00:04:01.724
We have Tina and Queenie Goldstein.

00:04:01.724 --> 00:04:05.604
I looked for those dresses in
my size, that didn't exist.

00:04:05.604 --> 00:04:07.862
Now, again, great things, guys.

00:04:07.862 --> 00:04:10.494
Oscar winners for best
costumes, Fantastic Beasts.

00:04:10.494 --> 00:04:12.148
If you haven't seen the movie, watch it

00:04:12.148 --> 00:04:13.730
and then come check all this stuff out.

00:04:13.730 --> 00:04:15.454
Now those are some of my favorite things

00:04:15.454 --> 00:04:17.484
from the Harry Potter
exhibit, but of course,

00:04:17.484 --> 00:04:19.220
we encourage you to come
see it for yourself.

00:04:19.220 --> 00:04:22.018
So book your tickets,
go to WBStudioTour.com

00:04:22.018 --> 00:04:24.160
and lay your eyes on these things too.

00:04:24.160 --> 00:04:25.743
We'll see you soon.

